From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Support ClientResponse stream_writer argument

aiohttp 3.14 requires a stream writer when constructing ClientResponse.
Mock its output size for completed requests, while retaining compatibility
with older aiohttp versions that do not accept this argument.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 aioresponses/core.py | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/aioresponses/core.py b/aioresponses/core.py
--- a/aioresponses/core.py
+++ b/aioresponses/core.py
@@ -188,6 +188,8 @@ class RequestMatch(object):
         kwargs['traces'] = []
         kwargs['loop'] = loop
         kwargs['session'] = None
+        if 'stream_writer' in inspect.signature(ClientResponse).parameters:
+            kwargs['stream_writer'] = Mock(output_size=0)
 
         # We need to initialize headers manually
         _headers = CIMultiDict({hdrs.CONTENT_TYPE: content_type})
